  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of the infinite series $1+\\frac{1}{2 !}+\\frac{1.3}{4 !}+\\frac{1.3 .5}{6 !}+\\ldots \\ldots$. is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "JVbXW",
      "text": "$e$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "G76UM",
      "text": "$e^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zhX1o",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{e}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HZ9Yb",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{e}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints : $\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{n}}=\\frac{1.3 .5 \\ldots(2 n-1)}{\\mid 2 n}$\n\n\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\frac{\\mid 2 n}{\\lfloor 2 n(2.4 \\ldots 2 n)} \\\\\n& =\\frac{\\lfloor 2 n}{2^{\\mathrm{n}}\\lfloor n \\mid 2 n} \\\\\n& =\\frac{x^{\\mathrm{n}}}{\\lfloor n} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\frac{x}{\\lfloor 1}+\\frac{x^2}{\\lfloor 2}+\\ldots=e^x-1 \\quad \\frac{1}{2}=x \\\\\n& \\exp =1+e^x-1=e^x=e^{1 / 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
